<<~ kanawai uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/ref/RFC-2119`>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! The face intent plane ~ the channel of intent through a face's fleet

''The daemon wiki reads pono; the operator and the AIs need a channel of intent through each PersonaGroup's fleet of device vessels'' (#/rulings). The research that read the field rests at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/face-intent-plane-2026`>>.

The model in one line: ''the daemon wiki keeps working memory; a face's intents travel on that face's own intent plane; a vessel's own records rest in its daemon bag.''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-split`>>

!! The split ~ each part of the daemon's work, and its home

|! Part |! Its home |! Why |
| The face's pins (group, signer, KEL prefix, device edge) | the face's custody and `@persona-<tag>` | identity belongs to the face; the floor reads none of them until the face's atom lights (`K15` step 2c) |
| The working-memory stage (`wikis/daemon/working`) | ''the daemon wiki, unchanged'' | the slate two minds leave things on before either knows where they belong, per vessel and per hand; it reads pono |
| Verb summonses and their answers | ''the face's intent plane'' (#/the-plane) | the channel of intent: addressed, answered by receipt, face-owned, clockless |
| Per-vessel records (boot outcomes, residency, alerts, claims in flight, local verbs' receipts) | the vessel's daemon bag, unmirrored | they belong to one vessel; one owner, the vessel |

The daemon wiki shows the intent plane through a read-only view: the pane where the operator and an agent watch intents and receipts flow. It never serves as the pipe.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-plane`>>

!! The plane ~ one face-owned, append-only log

* ''A fifth face plane'', `@intents-<tag>`, beside `@persona`, `@circles`, `@identities` and `@sessions` (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/automerge-tiga`>>). It derives from the PersonaGroup's tag like its siblings, so every device that joins the face derives its name and syncs it with no extra provisioning; two faces on one device share no entry; nothing stands above it. The PersonaGroup mints it and delegates append to each device edge; the mint order binds as for every face plane.
* ''Never mirrored'': the plane carries the control plane, so it never projects to the tracked tree (the daemon bag's own law, <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/wiki-layer-ontology`>>).
* ''Entries append, never edit'', each signed by the atom of the device that writes it (a far agent's by its own key, #/the-far-agent). Kinds:
** `intent`: an invocation naming its verb, its arguments, its audience and its causal bound (#/no-clock). Its id is the content hash of issuer, verb, arguments and nonce, so every device derives it offline and a replayed copy carries the same id. An idempotent verb takes the empty nonce.
** `outcome`: a receipt whose `cause` names the intent's id and whose signer names the device that acted.
** `asks` and `answer`: an outcome that needs a hand (a human approval, a missing capability) names what answers it; any session wearing the face answers by an entry citing the ask's id.
** `claim`, `release`, `takeover`: soft steering for a long act (#/who-answers); never safety.
** `supersede` and `cancel`: an issuer's or the operator's later word on an intent.
* ''The audience'' names one of four modes, as data: one pinned device (by atom), an ordered preference list of devices, a capability class (any device holding a named capability), or every device. A single-effect request that pins no executor issues only into an `asks` gate: an `answer` citing the ask names the executing atom, and a stray answer grants nothing. Per-device inboxes stay views of the plane, never storage.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/who-answers`>>

!! Who answers ~ stand-down first, idempotent effects as the floor, no election

The field holds no leaderless election for "any device of a fleet", and a lease cannot give mutual exclusion even with a clock: a paused holder still acts. So the plane never rests safety on a claim.

# ''Stand down on an outcome.'' Before acting, a device reads the plane for an outcome in its audience slot; where one stands, it does nothing.
# ''Safety lives in the effect.'' Every verb sorts into one of three classes, declared with the verb: ''idempotent or convergent'' (two answers harmless; keyed by the intent's id), ''per-device'' (its effect touches one vessel; one owner by construction), ''single-effect fleet-wide'' (two answers harm). The third class MUST NOT address "any device": an issuer pins its executor, or a human `answer` names the executing atom. An intent that breaks this refuses at issue.
# ''The winner reads, never elects.'' Where two outcomes stand for one slot after a merge, the outcome of the earliest device in the intent's own preference list counts; outside a list, the outcome whose `H(atom ‖ intent id)` reads lowest counts. Every other outcome stays in the log, marked a duplicate: the loser's act already happened, and its record stays visible.
# ''A claim steers effort'' on a long act: a claimant appends `claim`, then its outcome or `release`. Another device may append `takeover` naming the claim; a fenced effect accepts an act only from the current claim, and an idempotent one converges either way.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/no-clock`>>

!! No clock ~ nothing expires by time

* ''A claim never expires.'' It ends by its own outcome, by `release`, or by `takeover`. A device MAY suspect a claim stale by its own local elapsed time and decide to try a takeover; no clock value enters the log or settles anything.
* ''An intent voids by a causal event'' named in its bound: superseded by a later entry, its issuer's delegation revoked, the face's roster passing a named edge, or the operator's `cancel`. A device that merges the void before acting declines; one that acted before merging leaves a recorded act, never a silent loss.
* ''The operator's release always wins'': a `release` or `cancel` signed for the face outranks any claim, by authority, never by order.
* ''An `every` intent reaches a device that joins after it'', unless its bound names a roster edge; the reader evaluates the audience against the roster it holds.
* ''Compaction folds by the operator's act alone'': an answered intent and its outcomes fold into a summary entry when the operator runs the fold, never on a timer.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-far-agent`>>

!! The far agent ~ an AI that acts from afar

An agent off every device of the face (a cloud sandbox, another machine) never holds an atom: a shared act never makes a shared secret. The agent never wears the face's session either: a session meets one face and one anchor and carries a hand that acts as the face (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract#/the-hands`>>), while the agent acts as itself under a delegation the face signed.

* The agent holds its own key and a narrow delegation from the face: a verb prefix, an argument policy and a causal bound (`until` or `asOf` naming a signed roster act) in place of an expiry time. The persona root signs the grant at its epoch, and it lives only at the lineage's current root epoch.
* It signs an `intent` that references its delegation and hands it to a ''relay seat'': a vessel of the face with a door off the local socket on `INTENT_RELAY_ROUTE`, opened per face, ring-gated and off by default, with its enablement resting in a custody record. The relay decides on fresh authority, appends the entry unchanged with the AGENT's signature, and countersigns only its admission, a separate receipt under the relay's own key that lists as provenance and changes no status, `mayAct` or winner.
* The answering device signs the outcome with its atom, `cause` naming the invocation. A reader on a node or in a browser verifies agent → delegation → face, invocation → outcome, and atom → device edge → face, and trusts the relay for nothing after admission: a receipt under a valid relay key for an absent, revoked or out-of-prefix entry makes nothing act.
* A revoked delegation refuses on read, wherever the revocation arrives first; a pending sibling voids, and an act admitted before the revocation arrived stays recorded as revoked-after-acting.
* The kit reads what stands (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/i2-relay-lane`>>).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-vow`>>

!! The vow ~ an intent addressed to a face

''The lift.'' The plane's audience grows from device grain to face grain. A ''votum'' (plural ''vota'') names an intent addressed to a face: the vower issues it, the face's own actor drains it, and the outcome answers it. `intent` stays the wire kind, and the chain keeps its nouns: the verb, the summons that invokes it, the outcome that answers (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/verb-tiddler`>>). ''Receipt'' stays the ledger's word for what a vessel says about a request id (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/receipt-ledger`>>), and a votum's outcome never takes that name.

''Lineage.'' The vow grows from the operator's household and the hat-alignment keel, and from Freyja's vow, the operator's daughter's.

!!! Seven pattern integrities

# ''One object, many rotations.'' The Lararium shows each seat a face, and the shown face holds that seat's reality tunnel; one seat's turn never moves another seat's view.
# ''The vower binds itself; the face only admits.'' A seat's reach equals its grant, meeting the face's vow cap, meeting the face's own grants and lei; a votum's text requests, and caps grant.
# ''Later means the face's next causal turn.'' A votum voids by a causal event (supersede, cancel, revoke, a roster edge) and lapses by a counted number of the face's turns, never by time (#/no-clock).
# ''One face, one drainer, one turn.'' The face's lifecycle actor answers its vota one at a time; order holds within a face, and across faces only a named ref orders, a ref cycle refusing at issue.
# ''Effect once, outcome owed.'' The intent id hashes issuer, verb, arguments and nonce; a lost outcome retries as an outcome and never as the act, and an AI answer lands recorded once and never replays.
# ''Each enactor keeps its own lane.'' A deterministic votum never falls to an AI, and no votum reaches the hand-only class (promote, retire, unlock, kui) by attenuation, never by policy (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract#/the-hands`>>).
# ''The wave delivers; a new cause re-arms.'' Vota land on the nalu wave (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/nalu`>>), and an outcome never re-arms its own votum.

!!! Eight flows ~ what the house does with a votum

|! Flow |! Roman stage |! What it does |
| 1. Word | //concipere// | a seat issues an intent addressed to face F: verb, arguments, nonce, enactor, optional refs |
| 2. Admit | //suscipere// | F's door checks reach, refs and the hand-only class, then queues the votum or answers a void outcome naming the broken condition |
| 3. Bind | //voti reus// | a votum with refs waits until each named outcome lands; the others stand ready |
| 4. Answer | | on F's lit turn the actor drains ready vota one by one, `mayAct` first |
| 5. Pay | //solvere// | a deterministic votum runs its declared effect (oracle cast, ddate, cabalculate, grant landings, TW5 affordances); an AI votum reads the brief through F's tunnel from a seat holding F's standing and answers once, the house witnessing what it can check |
| 6. Inscribe | //V.S.L.M.// | a signed outcome names who paid (seat, face, on whose behalf), how it landed (void, landed, witnessed) and against what (intent id, lei spent) |
| 7. Read back | | the hearth roster at wake shows seats, rotations, lanes, open vota and unclaimed outcomes, and a votum stuck past its turn count shows stuck |
| 8. Withdraw | | the vower cancels, a revoke stops admission, and an admitted votum finishes or voids with its cause |

!!! What stands built, and what rests on the road

* ''Built.'' The plane and its entries, `mayAct`, the delegations a far agent carries, owed outcomes, and the door's `runDeclaredEffect` port for idempotent declared verbs (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/intent-*.ts`, `packages/lararium-keyhive/src/face-intent-door.ts`); the hearth roster's read of seats, rotations, lanes, open vota and owed outcomes at wake (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/hearth-roster`>>). Beside them:
** ''The face's turn.'' Each lit face stands its own door, keyed by its atom (`face-doors`), in one shape for every face. Each answer a door gives (a votum, or its owed outcomes) runs on a turn the face admits (`admitTurn`, shaped as the face actor's `admitWork`): a dark or closing face answers none, and the face's next lit turn heeds what waited. Where the actor admits the turn (`admitWork`), its close waits out the votum in flight. On the daemon island the face's drop does: the votum in flight lands under the face's own hive, then the door detaches and its planes leave the island's cache. The vessel's close reaches CLOSED without the island's answer (face-lifecycle), so its saves may drain before that votum's outcome lands; an outcome that misses the drain answers again at the face's next lit turn, which the door's declared effects keep whole, since a sibling's door pays idempotent declared verbs alone, with change coalescing kept. A face's light reaching the daemon island heeds that face's own door.
** ''A lit sibling's own door'' (operator ruling 2026-11-21). A sibling lit beside the worn face mounts its proven intents and persona planes in the live Repo for its lit life, and answers its vota under its own atom and through its own engine, never turning the worn slot. Four limits hold, each a test (`sibling-plane-mount`): the mount takes the intents and persona planes alone, and any other slot kind refuses; a pair its own signed log and verified KEL do not name mounts nothing, the vessel proving it at the light and the island re-reading it before either plane is read for a votum; the lit life bounds it, a close or a lock filing both documents under no face and dropping the mount whole while the door detaches; and every intent write names its face, a plane refusing an entry of another face (`intent-plane-misfiled`).
** ''The deterministic enactors.'' `ddate` and `oracle-cast` declare idempotent and pay through `runDeclaredEffect`, never through an AI. A declaration names the arguments it `fixes`, each one a thing its effect would otherwise draw for itself (chance, a time): a cast votum carries its time and the coins its issuer threw at the word, so every answer and every re-run lands the same cast, and a votum without them refuses `args-unfixed` at issue and on read. A declaration also names what it `bars`: an argument naming a draw of chance the effect would make for itself, so a calendar votum whose format names its `%.` exclamation refuses `args-draw-chance`, and every device that answers one votum lands the same text.
** ''The chore mark stays home.'' Each outcome a door lands keeps, beside it and never on it, the house-local `ChoreReceiptMark`: the face it answered as (its handle index here), the asker's hand `seat` (a seat of the face signed the votum, or the relay seat admitted it) and no session. The signed outcome keeps its cause, its signer and its result alone, so no handle index, hand or session crosses the plane, and no outcome pairs a requester with what it answered (`K20`, <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/verb-tiddler`>>).
* ''Rests on the road.'' `cabalculate`, which stands as no verb yet; the face-named vow cap (a standing lei: reach `standing`, scope seat, affordance and enactor); conditional refs; the AI enactor; a votum's turn count, so the roster names no votum stuck. Flow 3, flow 7's stuck reading and flow 5's AI branch therefore read as design until those land, and the pattern integrities above name the law each must keep.

''Cross-reads.'' The verb, summons and outcome records rest at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/verb-tiddler`>>; the ledger's facts at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/receipt-ledger`>>; the wave at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/nalu`>>; the hands that issue and answer at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract#/the-hands`>>. A votum may pay into a Votive, the bounty pool of <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/libation-pool#/the-wave`>>.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-rubric`>>

!! The rubric ~ what earns a place in a face's log

''Every little action stays out of a face's log'': each keystroke replaces a cached invariant tiddler in memory with another, so a draft mid-edit does not belong (#/rulings). The plane carries a hand's ''decisions that cross devices'', never its ''motion''. An entry belongs on the plane only when every test below holds:

# ''It crosses a device boundary.'' Its effect or its answerer stands on some device other than the one where the hand acts, or the fleet must read its outcome. An act whose effect and observers rest on one vessel leaves at most a receipt in that vessel's daemon bag.
# ''It settles.'' A hand committed it: save-and-publish, ask, approve, join, re-key, move a carrier's residency, grant, revoke. A keystroke, a cursor, a selection, a mid-edit draft, a cached invariant tiddler and every `$:/temp`, `$:/state` and `$:/status` title never qualify; they live in working memory and the volatile tiers.
# ''It acts on content; it never carries content.'' Content travels on its own bag's document and its own sync. The plane names a carrier by its address or CID and says what to do with it; a body never rides an entry.
# ''It expects an answer.'' An intent addresses someone and awaits an outcome. A broadcast of state that nobody answers belongs on a plane or document of its own, never here.
# ''Its authority matters later.'' Someone may ask who asked and who acted; the entry exists to answer that.

''Granularity'': one entry per decision, never per change. A session's edits coalesce in working memory, and the hand's commit turns them into one intent at most. ''Progress'': no heartbeats; between an intent and its outcome only `claim`, `asks` and their answers appear; progress detail rests in the acting vessel's own bag. ''Rate'': the plane's entry rate follows the rate of decisions by humans and agents, never the rate of input; a witness counts entries per committed act.

|! An act |! Where it goes |
| a keystroke in a tiddler | working memory; never written as an entry |
| a draft mid-edit | `wikis/<slug>/working` or the daemon wiki's working stage |
| saving a tiddler in the face's own wiki | that wiki's bag and its own sync; no intent |
| "move this carrier to the crossroads" | an `intent`, its `outcome` on the plane |
| "admit this new device to the face" | an `intent` pinned to the hearth that holds the root |
| an agent's request for approval | an `asks`, answered by a session wearing the face |
| a vessel's boot outcome | the vessel's daemon bag |
| `lares tiddler get --meme` on the local socket, touching that vessel alone | no entry; a receipt in that vessel's daemon bag |

''The myth'': the conch blows for decisions, never for breaths. The slate holds the chalk; the conch carries the call, names who should answer, and hears who did.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-reds`>>

!! The reds ~ what a test must show for the plane to hold

# Two partitioned devices both answer an idempotent intent addressed to a class; after the merge the effect equals one run, one outcome counts and both stand recorded.
# A device that merges an outcome for its slot before acting performs no effect (a spy on the effect).
# A pinned intent never runs on another device, though that device holds the capability.
# A single-effect fleet-wide verb addressed to a class refuses at issue; the same verb pinned, or named by a human `answer`, issues.
# A zombie claimant acts after a `takeover`: a fenced effect refuses its act, an idempotent one converges, and a clock injected to throw never gets read.
# A replayed intent keeps its id and draws no second effect; the control, a fresh nonce, draws a new id.
# An `every` intent draws one outcome per device, never one in all (dedupe stays scoped to the audience slot).
# Two faces on one vessel share no entry; a device that joins a face derives the plane and syncs it with no provisioning.
# A far agent's intent, admitted by a relay, verifies on a device that never saw the relay; a revoked delegation refuses on read, the revocation arriving first or after; a relay that alters an argument breaks the signature.
# A device asleep across a voiding event declines on waking; an intent with no bound gets honored.
# The plane never reaches the mirror (the tree-clean witness, with a projected wiki as its known positive).
# A single-effect intent runs once under a re-pin and a re-target: an outcome spends the slot, so no atom may act on the same intent again; two bodies under one intent id refuse `id-collision` and void every copy; the control, a same-body duplicate, stays a duplicate.
# An admission receipt names one digest of the heads the relay judged against, so the plane's growth never carries a receipt past the Noise bound; a `class` audience reads the device's own capability; a denial, an out-of-audience outcome and each refusal show in the pane with the entry id they concern.
# A relay admission rechecks the ring, the key chain and the delegation immediately before the final append and before each effect of a heed loop, from the current document; a revocation merged during an earlier effect stops the later ones.
# The rubric holds: a hundred keystrokes and one save in a face's wiki write no entry; one "move to crossroads" writes one intent and one outcome. A seeded duplicate-answer fixture trips the duplicate counter before a zero gets trusted.

<<~/ahu>>

